WEBVTT

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.750
When I was a child, I was a coward.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.080
Have you been well?

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.700
Nothing's changed around here.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.040
How's Nicole?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.080
You know she's in elementary school?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.200
Really? She's gotten so big.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.830
Yeah, but she's too well-behaved.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.750
Is that right?

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.750
I wasn't good at speaking with people,

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.000
and I would always hide
behind the shadow of my mother or a pillar.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.290
In terms of self-assertion,
the word "self" wasn't really there.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.790
You understand this?

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.290
Can I come over to play today?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.620
I want to come, too!

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.200
That's the kind of child I was.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.200
Sure! Let's all play together!

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.750
For the next section, Miss Saito?

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:55.330
Y-Yes.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:58.250
A-A... r-red...

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.700
I had a complex about the stutter
that would appear when I became nervous,

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.540
She's like a chicken.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.910
and I was teased a lot in class.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:20.910
Whenever I saw those cute,
fashionable girls that sparkled...

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:32.200
I, too, was standing on that glittering stage.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.120
It was at that time when I met her.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:42.330
My name is Miu Takigawa.
I look forward to learning with you all.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.830
"Chasing Our Dreams"

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.080
"EVENT CANCELLED"

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:43.540
The first time I saw Miu Takigawa,
I thought she was strange.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.620
She made that impression on me.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.120
--Can I sleep over at your house tonight?
--No.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.370
--Why?
--Because it isn't the weekend.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.950
She didn't seem to want
to join any of the groups.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.950
Miu, won't you play with us?

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:10.750
She would sit in the corner of the classroom
reading manga or books about music.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.750
I'm reading this.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.910
Oh, okay. Sorry for bothering you.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.910
Whenever someone would talk to her,
she didn't try to get along with them.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.500
What's with her?

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.540
She gives off a bad vibe!

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.540
I never wanted to talk to her
in the first place.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.040
That's how I felt.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:26.530
"OCTOBER 9"
"PLAY 'SNOW WHITE'"
"SNOW WHITE ROLE - 3 PEOPLE"
"WITCH ROLE - 1 PERSON"

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:29.450
Is there anyone who wants to play the witch?

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.490
"PLAY 'SNOW WHITE'"

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:33.040
--What? I wanted to be Snow White.
--I want to be Snow White, too!

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.450
"SNOW WHITE - 3 PEOPLE
WITCH - 1 PERSON"

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.660
Yeah, I think Nicole would be a good witch!

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.870
She never participates in our discussions,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.160
and before this,
she played the part of a tree.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.790
I feel so sorry for you!

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.120
That's right. You should do it, Saito!

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.330
Agreed!

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:59.290
I think Nicole's so happy to play the witch
and that's why she's so quiet!

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:03.040
Okay, well, I'll write you down for now.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.910
W-W... N-No.

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.910
"SNOW WHITE
SCRIPT"

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.250
They cast me... as the witch.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:22.080
She has so many lines.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.660
And songs, too?

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.080
Maybe I can try and do it.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.080
"Mirror, mirror on the wall...

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.910
...who is the fairest of them all?"

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.200
This should be good practice for you.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:54.000
I recommended you for the witch's part
because you can't speak out very well.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.830
Go. Go...

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.200
"Go, go," what?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.950
I can't even understand what she's sayin'!

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.000
Hang in there!

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:15.870
"MUSIC ROOM"

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:22.040
♪ Mirror, oh, mirror on the wall, oh, mirror ♪

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:35.450
♪ I am the queen,
who is the fairest of all in the land ♪

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:39.330
♪ A scarlet apple... ♪

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.700
M-Miu? Um...

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.040
This is the witch's song.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:03.700
♪ Mirror, oh, mirror on the wall, oh, mirror, ♪

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:16.120
♪ I am the queen,
who is the fairest of all in the land ♪

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:08.120
She was silent until the end,
not speaking a single word to me.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.700
But she played for me.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.410
That much, I understood.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.580
A play?

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.200
You want to do it?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.950
But I'm just the witch.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:34.370
What are you saying?
The witch's role is an important one!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:37.370
It really is! So hang in there, Nicole!

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.410
We'll definitely come to see it!

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:41.910
Yeah!

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.910
Okay.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.000
Mirror, mirror on the wall,

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.870
who is the fairest of them all?

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:17.620
That would be Snow White.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.080
What?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:23.500
Snow White is more beautiful than me?

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.160
Are you really sure about doing that?

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.700
Wouldn't it be a problem if she loses it?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:31.080
She's always so darn timid.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.750
Don't you want to see
what her reaction will be?

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:39.000
Hello, lovely maiden.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.000
How would you like this scarlet apple?

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.790
It's surely sweeter
than any other you've had before.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.200
Hello, madame apple seller.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.410
Please, give me one if they're that delicious.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:57.660
Oh, is that right? Then allow me to...

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.450
It's gone!

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:05.830
Nicole?

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.040
I wonder what's wrong?

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.870
The apple's gone!

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.410
What's wrong, madame apple seller?

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.700
Did something bad happen?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:27.450
Wait a second! What the heck are you doing?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.410
--That hurts! Stop!
--M-Miu!

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.700
Hey, Miss Takigawa, what are you...

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.120
Miss Takigawa!

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.870
What's gotten into you, Miss Takigawa?

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.700
The rest of the play was cancelled.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.290
Miss Takigawa!

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:52.870
Miu was harshly scolded
by her mother and our teacher.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.870
Please excuse us.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:58.200
However, it was clear
she had taken action for my sake.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:07.750
Soon after that, she transferred schools,
and I never even got to thank her.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.750
I want to be an idol!

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.950
Strangely enough, I gained courage.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:26.200
That's how I created my current self.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.290
Training was an incentive.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:36.290
Gradually, I developed confidence.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.290
I went to auditions over and over.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.660
"AMATEUR IDOL AUDITIONS
FAIL"

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.500
Sometimes I thought I was going to break...

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.330
...but whenever I closed my eyes...

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:54.120
I saw the image of Miu Takigawa
from that day.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:11.830
And so I was surprised
the day we were reunited.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:16.370
She seemed to not remember me at all.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:22.750
What was I expecting, anyway?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.580
Are you going out?

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.580
Y-Yeah.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:59.000
I'm going now.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.660
Have fun!

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:02.950
Yeah.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.250
Hang in there.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.960
"NO ENTRY ALLOWED"

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.200
It's moving!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.080
This room never changes, huh?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.250
Sakura?

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:20.120
I got kinda lonely, so I decided to come visit.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:21.910
You, too?

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.200
Yeah. I am.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.950
There really isn't anyone
here in the office at all!

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.950
It's like a haunted house!
My heart was pounding.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.080
Those clothes.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:35.750
Well, I couldn't really relax, so I changed.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.000
I think I understand that.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.950
You should change, too, Miu!

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.330
Huh? Me?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:50.290
Yep! It's really you!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.910
But it's so weird, isn't it?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:56.290
Even though you look so good in those clothes,
you never seem to have any confidence about it.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:59.500
Yeah.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:03.080
Compared to the start,
I don't hate these clothes like I used to.

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:08.080
Oh, yeah! Did you see Jun on the news?

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:10.950
I did! That was such a Jun thing to do!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.660
It's so strange.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.870
Even though were seeing each other every day.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.870
It's already been a month.
I wonder how everyone's doing.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:31.620
One year ago, everything started here.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.790
You guys.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.410
Everyone!

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:47.450
Hey, there!
How have you all been?

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:53.040
What the heck? It turns out everyone
was thinking the same thing after all.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:57.870
Though, I must say,
I'm surprised that we all met up here.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:03.620
This is our formation day, so I couldn't relax.
Before I knew it, I was here.

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:07.790
That's rich for someone who was just saying,
"I wonder if it's okay for us to enter?"

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:11.370
and, "We're not trespassers, are we?"
Such an upstanding citizen you are.

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:13.450
I told you, I'm a janitor!

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:15.830
Saito, you...

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:18.410
I was just passing by,

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:20.540
and that's when
they forced me to go with them.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.700
Really? Just passing by?

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.790
You were just passing by the zoo?

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:27.330
Wh-What's wrong with that?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:32.040
And with that, all of 22/7 is assembled!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:46.160
Wait. Why did we all change clothes?

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:48.370
Just go with it!

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:51.700
Even Ranran and Mew-Mew changed, too!

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:55.410
Coming here, we couldn't help
but become a matching set.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:58.160
It's like a class reunion, isn't it?

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.910
It is our formation day, after all.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.910
Yay! Yay!

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.910
So what have y'all been up to lately?

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.830
Here comes Takoyaki's tactless question.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.200
What? That's a standard question at a reunion!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.950
I went back to school.
I've been a bit behind in my studies,

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.410
so I had to make up for lost time with that.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:22.950
Well, being an idol was like my side hustle,
so I'm doing just fine.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.500
I've started swimming laps at the gym.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:30.080
I've been enjoying my time before I go back
to the States, seeing sights around the country.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:33.120
I've been searching for a new job.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.000
And I--

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.790
We know.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.450
What about you, Nicorun?

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:41.200
I haven't really been doing
anything to write home about.

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:45.120
But you told me
you were being picked up by another agency.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.580
Really? That's amazing!

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:53.540
You always did want to become an idol!
Congrats, Nicorun!

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.290
Thanks.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:59.580
Even if it's only been a month, hearing all
this, it feels like it's been longer than that.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:05.370
Because we were always together.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:14.910
Ranran, let's stop all this sad talk, yeah?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:17.160
After all, we all got together here.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.620
R-Right? Sorry about that!

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:25.200
We were finally all able to meet and all.
I've always wanted to thank you guys.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.790
That's our first photo shoot!

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:29.580
Yep!

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:33.070
"WEEKLY SHONEN MONDAY MAGAZINE"

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:33.620
Where we were surrounded
by cherry blossom trees.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.950
Our first pinup photo shoot.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.540
This book is my treasure.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.540
Thank you.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.290
Ranran.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.370
I, too, would like to show my gratitude.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:52.870
Our first concert
when we got the request for an encore...

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:54.580
...for no reason...

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:58.200
I felt as if I had been given a place to belong.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:03.290
It felt wonderful.

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.120
I know what you mean!

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.160
We practiced so much.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:11.500
When Akane first started to cry,
I almost started, too!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.000
I was so happy.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.120
When I was confused
about the swimsuit shoot,

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.120
even though I was leader,
I still said selfish things.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:31.870
But in the end, I was so glad
I was able to break out of my shell.

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:37.620
I love doing fun things.
I wanted to do so many of those!

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.000
Jun.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.580
I didn't know that being an idol
could be so much fun all the time!

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:55.410
I swear, y'all are such weird ducks.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:58.040
At first, all we did was fight,

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:01.700
but I think that's
one of y'all's strong points.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:06.870
I thought, "Even boorish girls like this
can become idols"!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.580
It allowed me to dream.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:13.910
All of you are such dummies.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:20.330
What about you, Christel?

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:25.450
And also the returnee girl
whose English I get sick of sometimes.

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:30.540
As well as the busy-body Takoyaki...

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.200
...and the kid who never gets nervous.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.250
The always-stuck-up Elizabeth.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.700
The too-serious
and stubborn upstanding citizen.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:45.500
The AI that can't read the room.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.830
It's been fun being with all of you!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.540
What the heck is with us?

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:22.200
I love you all so much.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.000
I really wanted...

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.410
...to continue on as 22/7 for a while.

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:57.500
Why?

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.910
Why did you help me?

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:04.160
It seemed like you'd break.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:10.790
If I'd let things go on,
if I'd stayed quiet and feigned indifference...

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:18.910
...it seemed like that would've broken
my most precious thing.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:23.700
Your most precious thing?

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:44.830
That's how she...

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.700
...has always been.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:53.450
If I have to do that in order to protect
the people most precious to me,

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.750
I'll become the world's top idol.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:58.080
I'll do anything!

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:08.080
I don't know what act she would commit to
protect the thing that's most precious to her.

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:13.080
That's the kind of person she is.

00:23:48.290 --> 00:23:51.830
E-E... E...

00:23:56.040 --> 00:24:00.200
E-Every... Everyone...

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:05.790
Welcome to 22/7.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:12.050
"Episode 12: 22/7"

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:12.000
"22/7."
